{"id": "EUVD-2026-95124", "enisaUuid": "33c7a77d-9a17-360a-aac8-3b250300ac03", "description": "FFmpeg through 9.0.2 contains an infinite loop vulnerability in ff_rtsp_connect() in libavformat/rtsp.c that follows RTSP 3xx redirects without any redirect limit. Attackers controlling an RTSP server can answer every request with a 302 redirect to itself or another server, causing endless reconnects that saturate a CPU core.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T17:30:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T11:41:54", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24902", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavformat/rtsp.c#L2225", "https://gist.github.com/OxBat/648a0bd60c898f2ffb418e131ce26013", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-through-9.0.2-infinite-loop-via-rtsp-redirect-handling-in-rtsp-c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jmpw-6qm3-5h67", "CVE-2026-107696"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f8a12c75-fa2a-3802-9a34-a3112639f4da", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.0.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "818d44bb-5cf2-3700-8636-13294775f0eb", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}